{"created": "2026-04-24T16:25:31.162441+00:00", "modified": "2026-04-24T16:25:31.632239+00:00", "id": 19738204, "conceptrecid": "19738203", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.19738204", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.19738203", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19738204", "metadata": {"title": "An Exploratory Transplant Assay for Attention Schema Theory in a Toy Neural Agent", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.19738204", "publication_date": "2026-04-24", "description": "<p>This preprint presents an exploratory, preservation-motivated transplant assay for Attention Schema Theory in a toy neural agent. A small neural network agent with separable attention, attention-schema, and self-model modules is trained in a grid-world task involving attention control, supervised self-report, and a theory-of-mind probe.</p>\n<p>The main result is mixed-negative. Exact copied self-model state survives transfer, as measured by source-specific fingerprint probes, but frozen schema transfer does not preserve strong self-report behavior across the tested architecture change. The theory-of-mind probe failed at this scale, and an exploratory Phi-star side analysis was inconclusive. The paper does not claim consciousness preservation; it frames the experiment as a small-scale engineering assay for testing preservation-relevant functional transfer.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Ryan, Thomas", "affiliation": null}], "keywords": ["attention schema theory", "mind preservation", "artificial consciousness", "self-model", "attention", "transplant assay", "computational neuroscience", "philosophy of mind", "consciousness", "neural networks"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.19374628", "relation": "references", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}], "version": "v1.0.0", "language": "eng", "custom": {"code:codeRepository": "https://github.com/Atomics-hub/consciousness-research", "code:programmingLanguage": [{"id": "python", "title": {"en": "Python"}}], "code:developmentStatus": {"id": "concept", "title": {"en": "Concept"}}}, "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "19738203"}}]}}, "title": "An Exploratory Transplant Assay for Attention Schema Theory in a Toy Neural Agent", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19738204", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/19738204", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/19738204?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19738204", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19738204", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.19738204", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19738204/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19738203", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/19738203", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19738203", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.19738203", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:19738204/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:19738204/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19738204/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19738204/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:19738204:ryan_2026_preservation_test_ast.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:19738204:ryan_2026_preservation_test_ast.pdf/full/%5E50,/0/default.jpg", "100": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:19738204:ryan_2026_preservation_test_ast.pdf/full/%5E100,/0/default.jpg", "250": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:19738204:ryan_2026_preservation_test_ast.pdf/full/%5E250,/0/default.jpg", "750": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:19738204:ryan_2026_preservation_test_ast.pdf/full/%5E750,/0/default.jpg", "1200": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:19